# A possible slide lies between two claims rather than within one. In S1, a part "must be perceived" in the sense that it exists only as perceived. In S2, "perceive" means "distinguish", that is, discriminate parts. A1 bridges these two senses. Each claim on its own keeps one sense in every statement that uses it.
